{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:bedf44c63f9023f9","name":"Hangar Bay","source":{"id":"source:reference-bedf44c63f9023f9","title":"Hangar Bay","revision":24995,"timestamp":"2024-11-10T16:55:12Z","sha256":"b441d98cb24775a264af8b42a3ca82eaa7e828b073d9efadad66810266a42120","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=24995","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Hangar%20Bay&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-bedf44c63f9023f9","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["HANGAR BAY\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["EP\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["AVAILABILITY\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SIZE RESTRICTION\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["COST\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Standard\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["8\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Colossal (Frigate) or Larger\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["10 (Base)\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Concealed\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["40\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Restricted"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Restricted"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Colossal (Frigate) or Larger\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1,000 (Base)\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["A Hangar Bay can be installed on a ship of Colossal (Frigate) size or larger. It holds secondary craft such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"}," or shuttles. Each bay has ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cost Modifier"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cost_Modifier"},"/50 units of hangar space, and multiple bays may be combined for more space. The hangar space taken up by a carried ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," is determined by its size: Huge, 1 unit; Gargantuan, 5 units; Colossal, 20 units. A ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," can enter or exit a Hangar Bay with two ",{"tag":"a","children":["Move Actions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Move_Actions"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Concealed Hangars:"]}," The presence of a Concealed Hangar isn't obvious to an external examination. Determine the hangar space as for a standard Hangar Bay, above. It takes a DC 30 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," check to recognize a Concealed Hanger for what it is from an external observation, though any thorough internal search of a ship reveals it. It takes two ",{"tag":"a","children":["Full-Round Actions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Full-Round_Actions"}," for a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," to exit or enter a Concealed Hangar Bay.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Jedi Counseling"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Web Enhancements"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Web_Enhancements"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Counseling"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Counseling"},")"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Q:"]}," Do nonflying carried ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," require Hangar Space? If so, it seems like the\n",{"tag":"a","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Imperial"]},"-Class Star Destroyer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Imperial-Class_Star_Destroyer"}," uses more Hangar Space for ",{"tag":"a","children":["AT-ATs"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/AT-ATs"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["AT-STs"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/AT-STs"}," than it does for ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighters"}," and shuttles.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["A:"]}," Hangar Space is required only for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," that are meant to launch directly from the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"},", such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Airspeeders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Airspeeders","referenceId":"reference:8831ac17fd67f6fc"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transports"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transports","referenceId":"reference:082a04e1f80578b3"},". If the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," is meant to be kept in storage until deployed planetside- as in the case of ",{"tag":"a","children":["AT-ATs"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/AT-ATs"}," and the like- then the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," can be carried as cargo. The real difference is that a hangar-deployed ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," is ready to fight when launched, but a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," carried as cargo needs a little help to become combat ready (usually about 1 minute of continuous work, assuming the Vehicle's entire crew assists).\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," stored in this way are still quite bulky (meaning they take up more cargo space than their mass would otherwise suggest). Nevertheless, this is considerably more efficient than allocating Hangar Space for the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"},", which includes enough room for maintenance, repair, takeoff, landing, and maneuvering. The precise amount of cargo space required is ultimately up to the GM, but a good baseline is that a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," requires about 100 tons of cargo space- roughly 50 cubic meters- for every unit of Hangar Space it would normally require. (As a comparison, this is about 1/4 as much room as the same ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," would require if you converted that cargo space into a Hangar Bay.)\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
